ms: the usage persist failures counter and builtinCatalog expiration are both confirmed through the ping mechanism and catalog updates. The catalog schema now includes the required fields across all protocol versions. I can't fully assess the model selection or provider reopening logic without seeing the relevant files, though the descriptions suggest those were addressed.\\n\\nFor the P4b-4 provider mutation issue, the fix changes the store commands to be async, releases the lock before making IPC calls, and uses a generation counter to prevent stale results. This approach separates the selection state protection from the actual IPC operations, which should prevent the original hang.\\n\\nOn the P4b-5 caching concern about PID-based keys, the brief correctly points out that when a new agentd process starts with a different PID, it correctly receives the necessary configuration rather than serving stale cached data—this is the intended behavior, not a problem. The brief also notes the existing tests already cover this scenario, though I don't have visibility into those test cases in this review.\\n\\nLooking at what the diff actually covers: the lock recovery mechanism is implemented with cross-host and PID reuse safeguards in place. Provider commands are properly async, the generation-based fencing is in place, and usage persist failures are tracked. However, several gaps remain—OAuth token persistence testing, lock recovery validation, and model selection logic aren't visible in the diff itself. Combined with the missing test files, I can't fully assess whether these scenarios are actually covered. Given the scope of what's missing, the review is incomplete.\\n\",\"thinkingSignature\":\"1d2144265e0c64ec35c728c1827f263252b256506fcdb7fa9c431f3ad929aa7e\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"\\n\\n## 审查结果\\n\\n**审查模式**：packet（无工具）\\n\\n**结论**：INCOMPLETE\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 范围与缺失材料\\n\\n本次 diff 包含锁回收机制、provider 异步命令、generation 围栏、用量持久化失败计数、`builtinCatalog` 更新、catalog schema 等改动。**未提供**以下关键材料，无法完成独立评审：\\n\\n| 缺失项 | 影响 |\\n|--------|------|\\n| 测试文件（含锁回收向量、OAuth 持久化验证、generation 代次测试） | 无法确认锁回收竞态、OAuth 写入文件、命令 superseded 场景的测试覆盖 |\\n| `pi-ai/src/auth/resolve.ts`（P4a-2 刷新写回凭据的实现位置） | 无法验证 OAuth 刷新后 token 是否真的落盘 |\\n| `agentd/src/models/runtime.ts` 变更前的 `apply` 方法 | 无法确认 `builtinCatalog` 是否在 apply 后同步刷新 |\\n| `provider/selection.rs` 变更前逻辑及 `provider_apply` 旧版本 | 无法确认 generation 围栏的必要性论证 |\\n| 沙箱外实测的完整测试输出（含 Node↔Rust 跨语言锁互通测试的具体用例描述） | 无法核实\\\"锁回收测试\\\"覆盖了哪些向量 |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 审查范围内的问题\\n\\n#### 1. 锁回收逻辑——`owner.json` 被删除但目录仍在时误判为存活\\n\\n**严重程度**：中  \\n**位置**：\\n- `agentd/src/models/credential-lock.ts:105`\\n- `src-tauri/crates/polaris-kernel/src/provider/credential_lock.rs:692`\\n\\n**证据**（Node 侧，Rust 侧逻辑相同）：\\n```ts\\n// credential-lock.ts:104-109\\nlet info: unknown;\\ntry { info = JSON.parse(await readFile(`${lock}/${token}/owner.json`, \\\"utf8`)); } catch { /* torn metadata */ }\\nif (!validOwner(info)) {\\n  const modified = await stat(`${lock}/${token}`).then((s) => s.mtimeMs).catch(() => undefined);\\n  if (modified !== undefined && Date.now() - modified > maxHoldMs) return retire(lock, token);\\n  continue;  // ← 目录有效但 owner.json 丢失时，age 也未超则跳过\\n}\\n```\\n```rs\\n// credential_lock.rs:692-693\\nlet info = fs::read(entry.path().join(\\\"owner.json\\\")).ok()\\n    .and_then(|b| serde_json::from_slice::<Owner>(&b).ok());\\nlet Some(info) = info.filter(...validOwner...) else { /* age check + continue */ };\\n```\\n\\n**可复现影响**：持锁进程在写入 `owner.json` 后、删除前崩溃，或文件系统元数据损坏导致文件消失；此时锁目录存在、`acquiredAt` 来自内存未落盘，无法通过时间判断。进程仍在运行时，`processState` 查询会返回\\\"alive\\\"，`reclaimable` 为 false，锁永久残留。**发生概率低但不可忽视**。\\n\\n**最小修复建议**：在 `acquire()` 中先写 `owner.json` 再原子 rename 到 lock 目录；或 `reclaim` 时检查目录年龄而非仅在 `validOwner` 失败时检查。\\n\\n---\\n\\n#### 2. `provider_apply` 中 `selected != id` 时提前返回\\n\\n**严重程度**：低  \\n**位置**：`src-tauri/crates/polaris-kernel/src/chat/backend/pi/mod.rs:397-398`\\n\\n**证据**：\\n```rs\\nlet (generation, selected) = crate::provider::selection::snapshot();\\nif selected != id { return Ok(serde_json::json!({\\\"applied\\\":false,\\\"superseded\\\":true})); }\\n```\\n\\n**分析**：若 `provider_switch` 已在 pending 状态但还未写入 `STORE.current_id`，此时 `selected` 仍为旧值，`provider_apply(\\\"new-id\\\")` 会直接返回 superseded，即使切换即将完成。这在以下时序下发生：\\n1. UI 触发 `provider_switch(\\\"claude-official\\\")`\\n2. Rust 侧 `changed()` 更新 generation，但 `STORE.current_id` 尚未写入（代码在 `let _mutation = PROVIDER_MUTATION.lock()` 之后才写）\\n3. 轮次内 `provider_apply(\\\"claude-official\\\")` 到来，`snapshot()` 拿到旧 id，返回 superseded\\n4. 循环重试，成功\\n\\n实际影响是增加一次 IPC 开销，不阻塞正确性。**低优先级**。\\n\\n---\\n\\n#### 3. `assertOwned` 在 Rust 侧 `write` 中的位置\\n\\n**严重程度**：低  \\n**位置**：`src-tauri/crates/polaris-kernel/src/provider/credential_file.rs:654`\\n\\n**证据**：\\n```rs\\n_lock.assert_owned()?;\\natomic_write(&path, &text).map_err(|_| \\\"CredentialStoreWriteFailed\\\".into())\\n```\\n\\n`assert_owned()` 在 `atomic_write` 之前调用。若锁在 `atomic_write` 执行期间被回收（竞态窗口），写入仍会完成但锁已失效。Node 侧在 `modify` 中先 `await assertOwned()` 再 `await save(root)`（`file-credentials.ts:208-209`），同样的窗口存在。\\n\\n**最小修复建议**：将 `atomic_write` 的目标路径纳入锁的原子性保护范围（例如写入临时文件后再 rename 到锁目录内），使写入本身与锁的生命周期绑定。\\n\\n---\\n\\n#### 4. 协议版本升级（5→6）的指纹测试覆盖\\n\\n**严重程度**：信息  \\n**位置**：\\n- `agentd/src/protocol/schema.ts:318` → PROTOCOL_VERSION = 6\\n- `src-tauri/crates/polaris-kernel/src/chat/backend/pi/protocol.rs:456` → 6\\n\\n**分析**：Node schema 和 Rust 协议版本同步升级到 6，新增字段 `usagePersistFailures`、`CatalogSchema`。根据 `protocol.rs:455` 注释\\\"fingerprint test gates changes\\\"，需确认指纹测试是否已更新。若无指纹测试约束，版本号升级无法防止未来两侧漂移。\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 建议验证步骤（区分推断风险与已有证据）\\n\\n| 步骤 | 类型 | 说明 |\\n|------|------|------|\\n| 补充锁回收向量测试：子进程持锁后被 SIGKILL，另一进程在 maxHoldMs 内回收并完成读写；活着进程不被抢锁；同时回收只有一个成功 | **推断风险** | diff 中未见测试文件，无法确认已有覆盖 |\\n| 补充 OAuth 持久化测试：使用 `FileCredentials` 登录后断言 `~/.polaris/credentials.json` 内容含新 token；刷新后再次断言文件更新 | **推断风险** | brief 称已补测试，但测试文件未提供 |\\n| 验证 `provider_apply` 提前返回场景：模拟 UI 切换 pending 期间轮次触发 | **推断风险** | 需要集成测试或日志验证 |\\n| 确认指纹测试已更新至协议版本 6 | **已有证据（diff）** | 两侧版本同步更新，但需实际测试确认 |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 结论说明\\n\\n本次 diff 实现了 P4a-1 锁回收机制的核心逻辑（持有者信息、墓碑原子重命名、PID/启动时间复用保护、跨主机超时），Node 与 Rust 两侧语义一致，generation 围栏解决锁内 IPC 阻塞问题。**但由于测试文件、OAuth 刷新写回实现、generation 必要性论证均未提供，独立审查无法确认以下关键项通过**：\\n\\n1. 锁回收在所有向量下正确（包括 owner.json 丢失但目录仍在的边界情况，见问题 1）\\n2. OAuth 刷新后 token 真的落盘而非仅在内存中\\n3. `builtinCatalog` 在 apply 后真的同步刷新\\n4. generation 代次\\\"最后一次选择生效\\\"的保证有测试佐证\\n\\n根据审查规则，**缺少必要实现或证据时使用 INCOMPLETE**，不能把未知当通过。\"}],\"api\":\"anthropic-messages\",\"provider\":\"minimax\",\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"usage\":{\"input\":19203,\"output\":4220,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"totalTokens\":23423,\"cost\":{\"input\":0.005760899999999999,\"output\":0.005064,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"total\":0.010824899999999998}},\"stopReason\":\"stop\",\"timestamp\":1791972800416,\"responseId\":\"071e88c2f0c5ffd0eb1d73b2c83149c1\"}],\"willRetry\":false}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
docs/execution/F1-1/events.jsonl:20:{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat agentd/src/sessions/registry.ts agentd/src/extensions/sandbox.ts\nsed -n '1,180p' agentd/src/daemon.ts\ncat src-tauri/crates/polaris-kernel/src/chat/backend/pi/mod.rs | head -150\ncat src-tauri/crates/polaris-kernel/Cargo.toml | head -100\nhead -45 docs/feature-tree.md\nrg -n 'F1|构建|no-default-features|cargo check' docs/pi-migration/*.md docs/feature-tree.md\nls docs/execution/F1-1\"","aggregated_output":"import { modelException } from \"../events/model-error.ts\";\nimport { recordUsage } from \"../events/usage-store.ts\";\nimport { Permissions, type Decision } from \"../extensions/permissions.ts\";\nimport type { SandboxResult } from \"../protocol/schema.ts\";\nimport { Sandbox } from \"../extensions/sandbox.ts\";\nimport { webFactory } from \"../extensions/web.ts\";\nimport { subagentFactory } from \"../extensions/subagent.ts\";\nimport { randomUUID } from \"node:crypto\";\nimport type { AgentSession, ExtensionFactory } from \"@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent\";\nimport type { Config } from \"../config/schema.ts\";\nimport { EventMapper } from \"../events/mapper.ts\";\nimport type { Models } from \"../models/runtime.ts\";\nimport type { ProtocolEvent, TurnStatus } from \"../protocol/events.ts\";\nimport { DaemonError, publicError } from \"../protocol/errors.ts\";\nimport type { SessionOptions, ImageAttachment } from \"../protocol/schema.ts\";\nimport { configureSession } from \"./options.ts\";\nimport { imagesForPrompt } from \"./attachments.ts\";\nimport { createSession } from \"./create.ts\";\n\ninterface Run {\n  id: string;\n  done: Promise<void>;\n  mapper: EventMapper;\n  stopped?: TurnStatus;\n}\ninterface Entry {\n  session: AgentSession;\n  rebuild: () => Promise<void>;\n  pendingReopen?: boolean;\n  pendingModel?: SessionOptions[\"model\"];\n  permissions: Permissions;\n  sandbox: Sandbox;\n  options: SessionOptions;\n  parent?: { id: string; callId: string };\n  depth: number;\n  children: Set<string>;\n  run?: Run;\n  lastStatus?: TurnStatus;\n  configuring?: Promise<void>;\n  toolProfile: string;\n  closing?: Promise<void>;\n  idle?: NodeJS.Timeout;\n  lastUsed: number;\n  queueReservations: number;\n}\n\nexport class SessionRegistry {\n  private readonly entries = new Map<string, Entry>();\n  private readonly opening = new Set<string>();\n  private pendingOpens = 0;\n  private runningChildren = 0;\n  private stopped = false;\n  constructor(\n    private readonly config: () => Config,\n    private readonly models: Models,\n    private readonly factories: ExtensionFactory[],\n    private readonly emit: (event: ProtocolEvent) => void,\n    private readonly usagePersistFailed: () => void = () => {},\n  ) {}\n  get size(): number { return this.entries.size; }\n  async open(sessionId?: string, cwd?: string, options: SessionOptions = {}, parent?: { id: string; callId: string }) {\n    if (this.stopped) throw new DaemonError(\"SHUTTING_DOWN\", \"Daemon is shutting down\");\n    if (sessionId && (this.entries.has(sessionId) || this.opening.has(sessionId))) {\n      throw new DaemonError(\"SESSION_ALREADY_OPEN\", \"Session is already open\");\n    }\n    if (this.size + this.pendingOpens >= this.config().maxSessions) {\n      throw new DaemonError(\"SESSION_LIMIT\", \"Maximum concurrent sessions reached\");\n    }\n    this.pendingOpens++;\n    if (sessionId) this.opening.add(sessionId);\n    try {\n      const config = this.config();\n      const state = { id: \"\" };\n      let permissions!: Permissions;\n      let sandbox!: Sandbox;\n      const assemble = (actualCwd: string): ExtensionFactory[] => {\n        const config = this.config();\n        permissions = new Permissions(options.permissionMode ?? config.permissions.defaultMode,\n          actualCwd, config.permissions.timeoutMs, config.permissions.summaryChars,\n          (approval) => this.extensionEvent(state.id, { event: \"permission.request\", targetSessionId: state.id, ...approval }),\n          (resolution) => this.extensionEvent(state.id, { event: \"permission.resolved\", targetSessionId: state.id, ...resolution }));\n        sandbox = new Sandbox(options.sandbox ?? false, actualCwd, config.sandbox,\n          (request) => this.extensionEvent(state.id, { event: \"sandbox.request\", targetSessionId: state.id, ...request }));\n        const factories: ExtensionFactory[] = [sandbox.factory(), webFactory(config.web, this.models.credentials),\n          subagentFactory((callId, task, signal) => this.subagent(state.id, callId, task, signal)),\n          (pi) => { pi.on(\"before_agent_start\", (event) => {\n            const prompt = this.entries.get(state.id)?.options.expertPrompt ?? options.expertPrompt;\n            if (config.experts.enabled) return { systemPrompt: [event.systemPrompt, config.experts.prompt, prompt].filter(Boolean).join(\"\\n\\n\") };\n          }); }, permissions.factory()];\n        return factories;\n      };\n      const session = await createSession(config, this.models, this.factories, sessionId, cwd, options, assemble);\n      state.id = session.sessionId;\n      if (this.stopped) {\n        session.dispose();\n        throw new DaemonError(\"SHUTTING_DOWN\", \"Daemon is shutting down\");\n      }\n      const parentEntry = parent ? this.entries.get(parent.id) : undefined;\n      if (parent && (!parentEntry?.run || parentEntry.run.stopped || parentEntry.closing)) {\n        session.dispose();\n        throw new DaemonError(\"TURN_CANCELLED\", \"Parent stopped while opening child\");\n      }\n      const id = session.sessionId;\n      const entry: Entry = { session, permissions, sandbox, rebuild: async () => {\n        options = { ...entry.options, ...(entry.pendingModel ? { model: entry.pendingModel } : {}) };\n        const replacement = await createSession(this.config(), this.models, this.factories,\n          undefined, entry.session.sessionManager.getCwd(), options, assemble, entry.session.sessionManager);\n        const previous = entry.session;\n        entry.session = replacement;\n        entry.options = options;\n        entry.pendingModel = undefined;\n        entry.permissions = permissions;\n        entry.sandbox = sandbox;\n        entry.pendingReopen = replacement.modelRuntime !== this.models.runtime;\n        previous.dispose();\n      }, pendingReopen: session.modelRuntime !== this.models.runtime, options: { ...options }, parent,\n        depth: parentEntry ? parentEntry.depth + 1 : 0, children: new Set(),\n        toolProfile: options.toolProfile ?? config.defaultToolProfile, lastUsed: Date.now(), queueReservations: 0 };\n      this.entries.set(id, entry);\n      if (parent) this.get(parent.id).children.add(id);\n      this.armIdle(id, entry);\n      return { sessionId: id, resumed: !!sessionId, messageCount: session.messages.length,\n        model: { provider: session.model!.provider, id: session.model!.id },\n        thinkingLevel: session.thinkingLevel, toolProfile: entry.toolProfile, tools: session.getActiveToolNames(),\n        reopenRequired: session.modelRuntime !== this.models.runtime };\n    } finally {\n      this.pendingOpens--;\n      if (sessionId) this.opening.delete(sessionId);\n    }\n  }\n  private get(id: string): Entry {\n    const entry = this.entries.get(id);\n    if (!entry) throw new DaemonError(\"SESSION_NOT_FOUND\", \"Session is not open\");\n    if (entry.closing) throw new DaemonError(\"SESSION_CLOSING\", \"Session is closing\");\n    return entry;\n  }\n  async configure(id: string, options: SessionOptions) {\n    const entry = this.get(id);\n    if (entry.pendingReopen && !entry.run && !entry.configuring) await this.reopen(id, entry);\n    if (entry.run || entry.configuring || !entry.session.isIdle) throw new DaemonError(\"SESSION_BUSY\", \"Session is busy\");\n    clearTimeout(entry.idle);\n    entry.configuring = configureSession(entry.session, this.config(), options);\n    try {\n      await entry.configuring;\n      entry.toolProfile = options.toolProfile ?? entry.toolProfile;\n      entry.options = { ...entry.options, ...options };\n      if (options.permissionMode !== undefined) entry.permissions.configure(options.permissionMode);\n      if (options.sandbox !== undefined) entry.sandbox.enabled = options.sandbox;\n      return { sessionId: id, model: entry.session.model && {\n        provider: entry.session.model.provider, id: entry.session.model.id },\n        thinkingLevel: entry.session.thinkingLevel, toolProfile: entry.toolProfile,\n        tools: entry.session.getActiveToolNames() };\n    } finally {\n      entry.configuring = undefined;\n      entry.lastUsed = Date.now();\n      if (entry.pendingReopen && !entry.closing && !this.stopped) await this.reopen(id, entry);\n      if (!entry.closing && !this.stopped) this.armIdle(id, entry);\n    }\n  }\n  prompt(id: string, text: string, attachments: ImageAttachment[] = []) {\n    const entry = this.get(id);\n    if (entry.run || entry.configuring) throw new DaemonError(\"SESSION_BUSY\", \"Use steer or followUp while a prompt is running\");\n    if (entry.pendingReopen) throw new DaemonError(\"SESSION_REOPEN_REQUIRED\", \"Session must be reopened before prompting\");\n    const images = imagesForPrompt(attachments, this.config());\n    if (images.length && !entry.session.model?.input.includes(\"image\")) {\n      throw new DaemonError(\"MODEL_IMAGES_UNSUPPORTED\", \"Selected model does not accept images\");\n    }\n    clearTimeout(entry.idle);\n    const mapper = new EventMapper(id, randomUUID(), (event) => this.emitEvent(id, event));\n    const run: Run = { id: mapper.turnId, mapper, done: Promise.resolve() };\n    entry.run = run;\n    // Reserve synchronously; start after the command returns to permit immediate abort.\n    run.done = Promise.resolve().then(() => this.execute(id, entry, run, text, images));\n    return { turnId: run.id, disposition: \"started\" };\n  }\n  private async execute(id: string, entry: Entry, run: Run, text: string, images: ImageAttachment[]): Promise<void> {\n    const { session } = entry;\n    run.mapper.emit({ event: \"turn.started\" });\n    const { turnIdleTimeoutMs, turnMaxMs } = this.config();\n    let idleTimer: NodeJS.Timeout;\n    let maxTimer: NodeJS.Timeout | undefined;\n    const expire = (code: \"TURN_IDLE_TIMEOUT\" | \"TURN_MAX_TIMEOUT\") => {\n      if (run.stopped) return;\n      run.stopped = \"timeout\";\n      clearTimeout(idleTimer);\n      clearTimeout(maxTimer);\n      run.mapper.error(code, code === \"TURN_IDLE_TIMEOUT\" ? \"本轮长时间未收到事件，已取消。\" : \"本轮超过最长运行时间，已取消。\");\n      this.cancelTools(entry);\n      void this.stopChildren(entry);\n      session.clearQueue();\n      void session.abort().catch(() => undefined);\n    };\n    const armIdle = () => {\n      clearTimeout(idleTimer);\n      if (!run.stopped) idleTimer = setTimeout(() => expire(\"TURN_IDLE_TIMEOUT\"), turnIdleTimeoutMs);\n    };\n    let usageOrdinal = 0;\n    const unsubscribe = session.subscribe((event) => {\n      armIdle(); // All SDK events count, including tool progress and retry/compaction events.\n      if (event.type === \"message_end\" && event.message.role === \"assistant\") {\n        try { recordUsage(this.config().usageDir, id, run.id, usageOrdinal++, event.message, session.modelRuntime); }\n        catch {\n          this.usagePersistFailed();\n          run.mapper.error(\"USAGE_PERSIST_FAILED\", \"Usage record could not be persisted\");\n        }\n      }\n      run.mapper.accept(event, !!run.stopped);\n    });\n    armIdle();\n    if (turnMaxMs > 0) maxTimer = setTimeout(() => expire(\"TURN_MAX_TIMEOUT\"), turnMaxMs);\n    try {\n      if (!run.stopped) {\n        await session.prompt(text, {\n          expandPromptTemplates: false, images,\n          preflightResult: () => {\n            if (run.stopped) throw new DaemonError(\"TURN_CANCELLED\", \"Turn was cancelled during preparation\");\n          },\n        });\n      }\n    } catch (error) {\n      if (!run.stopped) {\n        run.mapper.status = \"error\";\n        const safe = modelException(error) ?? publicError(error);\n        run.mapper.error(safe.code, safe.message);\n      }\n    } finally {\n      clearTimeout(idleTimer!);\n      clearTimeout(maxTimer);\n      unsubscribe();\n      this.cancelTools(entry);\n      await this.stopChildren(entry);\n      session.clearQueue();\n      entry.lastStatus = run.stopped ?? run.mapper.status;\n      entry.run = undefined;\n      entry.lastUsed = Date.now();\n      if (entry.pendingReopen && !entry.closing && !this.stopped) {\n        try { await this.reopen(id, entry); }\n        catch { run.mapper.error(\"SESSION_REOPEN_FAILED\", \"Provider configuration will be retried before the next turn\"); }\n      }\n      run.mapper.emit({ event: \"turn.completed\", status: run.stopped ?? run.mapper.status });\n      if (!entry.closing && !this.stopped) this.armIdle(id, entry);\n    }\n  }\n  async queue(id: string, text: string, method: \"steer\" | \"followUp\") {\n    const entry = this.get(id);\n    const run = entry.run;\n    if (!run || run.stopped) throw new DaemonError(\"SESSION_NOT_RUNNING\", \"No active turn accepts queued input\");\n    if (!entry.session.isStreaming) throw new DaemonError(\"TURN_NOT_READY\", \"Turn is still preparing\");\n    if (entry.session.pendingMessageCount + entry.queueReservations >= this.config().maxQueuedMessages) {\n      throw new DaemonError(\"QUEUE_LIMIT\", \"Maximum queued messages reached\");\n    }\n    entry.queueReservations++;\n    try {\n      const disposition = await entry.session[method](text);\n      return { turnId: run.id, disposition };\n    } finally {\n      entry.queueReservations--;\n      if (entry.run !== run || run.stopped) entry.session.clearQueue();\n    }\n  }\n  async abort(id: string): Promise<{ aborted: boolean }> {\n    const entry = this.get(id);\n    const run = entry.run;\n    if (!run) return { aborted: false };\n    run.stopped ??= \"aborted\";\n    this.cancelTools(entry);\n    await this.stopChildren(entry);\n    entry.session.clearQueue();\n    await entry.session.abort();\n    await run.done;\n    return { aborted: true };\n  }\n  async wait(id: string): Promise<void> { await this.get(id).run?.done; }\n  async close(id: string): Promise<void> {\n    const entry = this.entries.get(id);\n    if (!entry) throw new DaemonError(\"SESSION_NOT_FOUND\", \"Session is not open\");\n    if (entry.closing) return entry.closing;\n    clearTimeout(entry.idle);\n    if (entry.run) entry.run.stopped ??= \"aborted\";\n    this.cancelTools(entry);\n    entry.closing = (async () => {\n      try {\n        await entry.configuring?.catch(() => undefined);\n        entry.session.clearQueue();\n        const aborted = entry.session.abort();\n        await Promise.all([...entry.children].map((child) => this.close(child)));\n        await aborted;\n        await entry.run?.done;\n      } finally {\n        entry.session.dispose();\n        this.entries.delete(id);\n        if (entry.parent) this.entries.get(entry.parent.id)?.children.delete(id);\n      }\n    })();\n    return entry.closing;\n  }\n  private armIdle(id: string, entry: Entry): void {\n    clearTimeout(entry.idle);\n    const remaining = Math.max(1, this.config().idleTimeoutMs - (Date.now() - entry.lastUsed));\n    entry.idle = setTimeout(() => { void this.close(id).catch(() => undefined); }, remaining);\n    entry.idle.unref();\n  }\n  private cancelTools(entry: Entry): void {\n    entry.permissions.cancel();\n    entry.sandbox.cancel();\n  }\n  private async stopChildren(entry: Entry): Promise<void> {\n    await Promise.all([...entry.children].map((child) => this.abort(child).catch(() => undefined)));\n  }\n  private extensionEvent(id: string, payload: Parameters<EventMapper[\"emit\"]>[0]): void {\n    const run = this.get(id).run;\n    if (!run || (run.stopped && payload.event !== \"permission.resolved\")) throw new DaemonError(\"TURN_CANCELLED\", \"No active turn\");\n    run.mapper.emit(payload);\n  }\n  private emitEvent(id: string, event: ProtocolEvent): void {\n    const parent = this.entries.get(id)?.parent;\n    if (parent) {\n      if (![\"tool.started\", \"tool.completed\", \"permission.request\", \"permission.resolved\", \"sandbox.request\"].includes(event.event)) return;\n      const run = this.entries.get(parent.id)?.run;\n      if (run) this.emitEvent(parent.id, { ...event, sessionId: parent.id,\n        turnId: run.id, parentCallId: event.parentCallId ?? parent.callId });\n    } else this.emit(event);\n  }\n  respondPermission(id: string, callId: string, decision: Decision) {\n    if (!this.get(id).permissions.respond(callId, decision)) throw new DaemonError(\"APPROVAL_NOT_FOUND\", \"Approval expired or does not belong to this session\");\n    return { accepted: true };\n  }\n  respondSandbox(id: string, callId: string, result: SandboxResult) {\n    if (!this.get(id).sandbox.respond(callId, result)) throw new DaemonError(\"SANDBOX_REQUEST_NOT_FOUND\", \"Sandbox request expired\");\n    return { accepted: true };\n  }\n  async subagent(id: string, callId: string, task: string, signal?: AbortSignal): Promise<string> {\n    const entry = this.get(id);\n    const limits = this.config().subagents;\n    if (entry.depth >= limits.maxDepth) throw new DaemonError(\"SUBAGENT_DEPTH_LIMIT\", \"Maximum subagent depth reached\");\n    if (this.runningChildren >= limits.maxConcurrent) throw new DaemonError(\"SUBAGENT_CONCURRENCY_LIMIT\", \"Maximum concurrent subagents reached\");\n    if (signal?.aborted || !entry.run || entry.run.stopped) throw new DaemonError(\"TURN_CANCELLED\", \"Parent turn is not active\");\n    this.runningChildren++;\n    let childId: string | undefined;\n    const abort = () => { if (childId) void this.abort(childId).catch(() => undefined); };\n    signal?.addEventListener(\"abort\", abort, { once: true });\n    try {\n      const child = await this.open(undefined, entry.session.sessionManager.getCwd(), {\n        ...entry.options, toolProfile: entry.toolProfile,\n        model: entry.session.model && { provider: entry.session.model.provider, id: entry.session.model.id },\n        thinkingLevel: entry.options.thinkingLevel, permissionMode: entry.permissions.mode, sandbox: entry.sandbox.enabled,\n      }, { id, callId });\n      childId = child.sessionId;\n      if (signal?.aborted || entry.run?.stopped || entry.closing) throw new DaemonError(\"TURN_CANCELLED\", \"Parent cancelled while opening child\");\n      this.prompt(childId, task);\n      await this.wait(childId);\n      if (signal?.aborted || entry.run?.stopped) throw new DaemonError(\"TURN_CANCELLED\", \"Parent cancelled\");\n      const childEntry = this.get(childId);\n      if (childEntry.lastStatus !== \"completed\") throw new DaemonError(\"SUBAGENT_FAILED\", \"Child did not complete successfully\");\n      const messages = childEntry.session.messages;\n      const last = [...messages].reverse().find((message) => message.role === \"assistant\");\n      if (!last || last.role !== \"assistant\" || last.stopReason === \"error\" || last.stopReason === \"aborted\") {\n        throw new DaemonError(\"SUBAGENT_FAILED\", \"Child did not complete successfully\");\n      }\n      return last.content.filter((part) => part.type === \"text\").map((part) => part.text).join(\"\\n\").slice(0, limits.summaryChars);\n    } finally {\n      signal?.removeEventListener(\"abort\", abort);\n      if (childId) await this.close(childId).catch(() => undefined);\n      this.runningChildren--;\n    }\n  }\n  reopenRequired(): string[] {\n    return [...this.entries].filter(([, entry]) => entry.session.modelRuntime !== this.models.runtime)\n      .map(([id]) => id);\n  }\n  private async reopen(id: string, entry: Entry): Promise<void> {\n    clearTimeout(entry.idle);\n    entry.configuring = entry.rebuild();\n    try { await entry.configuring; }\n    finally {\n      entry.configuring = undefined;\n      if (!entry.closing && !this.stopped) this.armIdle(id, entry);\n    }\n  }\n  async refreshConfig(defaultChanged = false): Promise<void> {\n    for (const [id, entry] of this.entries) {\n      entry.pendingReopen = entry.session.modelRuntime !== this.models.runtime;\n      if (defaultChanged) entry.pendingModel = this.config().defaultModel;\n      if (!entry.run && !entry.configuring && !entry.closing) {\n        try { await this.reopen(id, entry); }\n        catch { /* Keep pendingReopen; config.apply reports unresolved sessions. */ }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  async shutdown(): Promise<void> {\n    this.stopped = true;\n    await Promise.all([...this.entries.keys()].map((id) => this.close(id)));\n  }\n}\nimport type { Config } from \"../config/schema.ts\";\nimport type { SandboxResult } from \"../protocol/schema.ts\";\nimport { randomUUID } from \"node:crypto\";\nimport {\n  createBashToolDefinition, createWriteToolDefinition, createEditToolDefinition,\n  type ExtensionFactory,\n} from \"@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent\";\n\nexport interface SandboxRequest { callId: string; operation: string; args: Record<string, unknown> }\nconst failure = (error: string): SandboxResult => ({ output: \"\", exitCode: null, signal: null, timedOut: false, error });\nexport class Sandbox {\n  private readonly pending = new Map<string, (result: SandboxResult) => void>();\n  private probe?: Promise<void>;\n  private cached?: { until: number; error?: Error };\n  constructor(public enabled: boolean, private readonly cwd: string, private readonly config: Config[\"sandbox\"],\n    private readonly emit: (request: SandboxRequest) => void) {}\n  respond(callId: string, result: SandboxResult): boolean {\n    const finish = this.pending.get(callId);\n    if (!finish) return false;\n    finish(result);\n    return true;\n  }\n  cancel(): void {\n    for (const finish of this.pending.values()) finish(failure(\"SANDBOX_ABORTED\"));\n  }\n  async available(): Promise<void> {\n    if (this.cached && Date.now() < this.cached.until) {\n      if (this.cached.error) throw this.cached.error;\n      return;\n    }\n    if (!this.probe) {\n      this.probe = this.exchange(\"probe\", {}, undefined, this.config.probeTimeoutMs).then((result) => {\n        if (result.exitCode !== 0 || result.timedOut || result.signal) throw new Error(\"Probe failed\");\n        this.cached = { until: Date.now() + this.config.probeCacheMs };\n      }).catch((cause: unknown) => {\n        const error = new Error(`SANDBOX_UNAVAILABLE: ${String(cause)}`);\n        this.cached = { until: Date.now() + this.config.probeCacheMs, error };\n        throw error;\n      }).finally(() => { this.probe = undefined; });\n    }\n    return this.probe;\n  }\n  async request(operation: string, args: Record<string, unknown>, signal?: AbortSignal): Promise<SandboxResult> {\n    await this.available();\n    return this.exchange(operation, args, signal, this.config.timeoutMs);\n  }\n  private exchange(operation: string, args: Record<string, unknown>, signal: AbortSignal | undefined,\n    timeoutMs: number): Promise<SandboxResult> {\n    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n      if (signal?.aborted) return reject(new Error(\"SANDBOX_ABORTED\"));\n      const callId = randomUUID();\n      const abort = () => finish(failure(\"SANDBOX_ABORTED\"));\n      const timer = setTimeout(() => finish(failure(\"SANDBOX_TIMEOUT: no host execution result\")), timeoutMs);\n      const finish = (result: SandboxResult) => {\n        clearTimeout(timer);\n        signal?.removeEventListener(\"abort\", abort);\n        this.pending.delete(callId);\n        if (result.error) reject(new Error(result.error)); else resolve(result);\n      };\n      this.pending.set(callId, finish);\n      signal?.addEventListener(\"abort\", abort, { once: true });\n      try { this.emit({ callId, operation, args: { ...args, cwd: this.cwd, ...this.config, timeoutMs } }); }\n      catch { finish(failure(\"SANDBOX_UNAVAILABLE\")); }\n    });\n  }\n  factory(): ExtensionFactory {\n    return (pi) => {\n      // Probe even before read-only/custom tools in a sandbox-enabled session.\n      pi.on(\"tool_call\", async () => {\n        if (!this.enabled) return;\n        try { await this.available(); }\n        catch (error) { return { block: true, reason: String(error) }; }\n      });\n      const file = async (operation: string, args: Record<string, unknown>) => {\n        const result = await this.request(operation, args);\n        if (result.timedOut || result.signal || result.exitCode !== 0) throw new Error(\"SANDBOX_EXEC_FAILED\");\n        return result.output;\n      };\n      const writeFile = async (path: string, content: string) => { await file(\"write\", { path, content }); };\n      const remoteWrite = createWriteToolDefinition(this.cwd, { operations: {\n        writeFile, mkdir: async (path) => { await file(\"mkdir\", { path }); },\n      } });\n      const remoteEdit = createEditToolDefinition(this.cwd, { operations: {\n        writeFile, readFile: async (path) => Buffer.from(await file(\"read\", { path }), \"base64\"),\n        access: async (path) => { await file(\"access\", { path }); },\n      } });\n      const remoteBash = createBashToolDefinition(this.cwd, { exposeSessionEnvironment: false, operations: {\n        exec: async (command, _cwd, options) => {\n          const result = await this.request(\"bash\", { command, timeout: options.timeout }, options.signal);\n          options.onData(Buffer.from(result.output));\n          if (result.timedOut) options.onData(Buffer.from(\"\\nSANDBOX_TIMEOUT\\n\"));\n          if (result.signal) options.onData(Buffer.from(`\\nSANDBOX_SIGNAL: ${result.signal}\\n`));\n          return result;\n        },\n      } });\n      const write = createWriteToolDefinition(this.cwd);\n      const edit = createEditToolDefinition(this.cwd);\n      const bash = createBashToolDefinition(this.cwd);\n      pi.registerTool({ ...write, execute: (...args) => (this.enabled ? remoteWrite : write).execute(...args) });\n      pi.registerTool({ ...edit, execute: (...args) => (this.enabled ? remoteEdit : edit).execute(...args) });\n      pi.registerTool({ ...bash, execute: (...args) => (this.enabled ? remoteBash : bash).execute(...args) });\n    };\n  }\n}\nimport { Value } from \"typebox/value\";\nimport type { ExtensionFactory } from \"@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent\";\nimport { mergeConfig } from \"./config/load.ts\";\nimport { ConfigPatchSchema, type Config } from \"./config/schema.ts\";\nimport { validateConfig } from \"./config/validate.ts\";\nimport { extensionFactories } from \"./extensions/index.ts\";\nimport { Logger } from \"./log.ts\";\nimport { memoryCredentials, Redactor, type CredentialStore } from \"./models/credentials.ts\";\nimport { Models } from \"./models/runtime.ts\";\nimport { DaemonError, publicError } from \"./protocol/errors.ts\";\nimport type { ProtocolEvent } from \"./protocol/events.ts\";\nimport { RequestSchema, type Catalog, type Request, type Response } from \"./protocol/schema.ts\";\nimport { versions } from \"./protocol/version.ts\";\nimport { validateAttachments } from \"./sessions/attachments.ts\";\nimport { SessionRegistry } from \"./sessions/registry.ts\";\n\nimport { Logins } from \"./models/logins.ts\";\n\nexport class Daemon {\n  private usagePersistFailures = 0;\n  readonly logins: Logins;\n  readonly sessions: SessionRegistry;\n  private readonly queues = new Map<string, Promise<void>>();\n  private readonly pending = new Set<Promise<void>>();\n  private stopping = false;\n  private shutdownTask?: Promise<void>;\n  private constructor(\n    public config: Config,\n    readonly models: Models,\n    readonly logger: Logger,\n    send: (value: ProtocolEvent | Response) => void,\n    factories: ExtensionFactory[],\n  ) {\n    this.logins = new Logins(models, () => this.config.oauthTimeoutMs);\n    this.sessions = new SessionRegistry(() => this.config, models, factories,\n      (event) => send(models.redactor.clean(event)), () => {\n        this.usagePersistFailures++;\n        this.logger.log(\"warn\", \"Usage record could not be persisted\", {\n          code: \"USAGE_PERSIST_FAILED\", usagePersistFailures: this.usagePersistFailures,\n        });\n      });\n  }\n  static async create(config: Config, send: (value: ProtocolEvent | Response) => void,\n    log: (line: string) => void, options: {\n      credentials?: CredentialStore; redactor?: Redactor; factories?: ExtensionFactory[];\n    } = {}): Promise<Daemon> {\n    const redactor = options.redactor ?? new Redactor();\n    const models = await Models.create(config, options.credentials ?? memoryCredentials(), redactor);\n    let daemon: Daemon;\n    const logger = new Logger(() => daemon?.config.logLevel ?? config.logLevel, redactor, log);\n    daemon = new Daemon(config, models, logger, send, options.factories ?? extensionFactories);\n    return daemon;\n  }\n  async handle(value: unknown): Promise<Response> {\n    const raw = value && typeof value === \"object\" ? value as Record<string, unknown> : {};\n    const id = typeof raw.id === \"string\" && raw.id.length || Number.isInteger(raw.id)\n      ? raw.id as string | number : null;\n    let sessionId: string | undefined;\n    try {\n      if (raw.method === \"config.apply\" && raw.params && typeof raw.params === \"object\" && \"config\" in raw.params) {\n        validateConfig(ConfigPatchSchema, raw.params.config);\n      }\n      if (raw.method === \"prompt\" && raw.params && typeof raw.params === \"object\" && \"attachments\" in raw.params) {\n        validateAttachments(raw.params.attachments, this.config);\n      }\n      if (!Value.Check(RequestSchema, value)) {\n        throw new DaemonError(raw.method === \"config.apply\" ? \"INVALID_CONFIG\" : \"INVALID_REQUEST\",\n          \"Request does not match schema\");\n      }\n      const request: Request = value;\n      sessionId = \"sessionId\" in request.params ? request.params.sessionId : undefined;\n      this.logger.log(\"debug\", \"Request received\", { requestId: request.id, sessionId });\n      if (this.stopping) throw new DaemonError(\"SHUTTING_DOWN\", \"Daemon is shutting down\");\n      const key = request.method.endsWith(\".respond\") ? undefined : sessionId ? `session:${sessionId}` : request.method === \"config.apply\" ? \"config\" : undefined;\n      const result = await this.schedule(key, () => this.dispatch(request));\n      this.logger.log(\"info\", \"Request completed\", { requestId: request.id, sessionId });\n      return { type: \"response\", id: request.id, ok: true, result };\n    } catch (error) {\n      const safe = publicError(error);\n      this.logger.log(\"warn\", \"Request failed\", { requestId: id ?? undefined, sessionId, code: safe.code });\n      return { type: \"response\", id, ok: false, error: safe };\n    }\n  }\n  private schedule(key: string | undefined, work: () => Promise<unknown>): Promise<unknown> {\n    const previous = key ? this.queues.get(key) : undefined;\n    const task = previous ? previous.then(work) : work();\n    const settled = task.then(() => undefined, () => undefined);\n    this.pending.add(settled);\n    if (key) this.queues.set(key, settled);\n    void settled.then(() => {\n      this.pending.delete(settled);\n      if (key && this.queues.get(key) === settled) this.queues.delete(key);\n    });\n    return task;\n  }\n  private async dispatch(request: Request): Promise<unknown> {\n    switch (request.method) {\n      case \"provider.auth\": return this.logins.handle(request.params.provider, request.params.operation, request.params.input);\n      case \"permission.respond\": return this.sessions.respondPermission(request.params.sessionId, request.params.callId, request.params.decision);\n      case \"sandbox.respond\": return this.sessions.respondSandbox(request.params.sessionId, request.params.callId, request.params);\n      case \"ping\": return { experts: { ...this.config.experts }, status: \"ok\", sessions: this.sessions.size, usagePersistFailures: this.usagePersistFailures, ...versions };\n      case \"models.list\": return { models: this.models.list() };\n      case \"models.catalog\": return { models: this.models.builtinCatalog } satisfies Catalog;\n      case \"session.open\": return this.sessions.open(request.params.sessionId, request.params.cwd, request.params);\n      case \"session.configure\": return this.sessions.configure(request.params.sessionId, request.params);\n      case \"prompt\": return this.sessions.prompt(request.params.sessionId, request.params.text, request.params.attachments);\n      case \"steer\":\n      case \"followUp\": return this.sessions.queue(request.params.sessionId, request.params.text, request.method);\n      case \"abort\": return this.sessions.abort(request.params.sessionId);\n      case \"close\":\n        await this.sessions.close(request.params.sessionId);\n        return { closed: true };\n      case \"config.apply\": {\n        const config = mergeConfig(this.config, request.params.config ?? {});\n        await this.models.apply(config, request.params.credentials);\n        const defaultChanged = JSON.stringify(this.config.defaultModel) !== JSON.stringify(config.defaultModel);\n        this.config = config;\n        await this.sessions.refreshConfig(defaultChanged);\n        // No config echo: credentials can also be embedded in endpoint URLs.\n        return { applied: true, reopenRequired: this.sessions.reopenRequired() };\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  shutdown(): Promise<void> {\n    this.stopping = true;\n    return this.shutdownTask ??= (async () => {\n      await this.logins.shutdown();\n      await Promise.all(this.pending);\n      await this.sessions.shutdown();\n    })();\n  }\n}\n//! Shared daemon adapter. Per-account fails closed until the shell can supply\n//! authenticated OS isolation; different working directories are not a sandbox.\nmod client;\nmod experts;\nmod process;\npub mod protocol;\nmod routes;\nmod sessions;\nmod input;\n#[cfg(test)] mod extension_tests;\n#[cfg(test)] mod wiki_tests;\nmod supervisor;\nmod translate;\n#[cfg(windows)] mod windows_job;\n#[cfg(test)] mod tests;\nuse super::*;\nuse client::{Client, Control};\nuse protocol::{Command, Empty, Prompt};\nuse parking_lot::Mutex;\nuse std::{collections::HashSet, sync::mpsc};\nuse serde_json::Value;\n\npub struct PiBackend {\n    config: config::Agentd,\n    client: once_cell::sync::OnceCell<Arc<Client>>,\n    preparing: Arc<Mutex<HashSet<String>>>,\n    cancelled: Arc<Mutex<HashSet<String>>>,\n    expert_lock: Mutex<()>,\n    provider_config: Mutex<Option<(Option<u32>, Value)>>,\n}\nimpl PiBackend {\n    pub fn new(config: config::Agentd) -> anyhow::Result<Self> {\n        config::Config { agent: config::Agent::default(), agentd: config.clone() }.validate()?;\n        let backend = Self { config, client: once_cell::sync::OnceCell::new(),\n            provider_config: Mutex::new(None), expert_lock: Mutex::new(()),\n            preparing: Arc::new(Mutex::new(HashSet::new())), cancelled: Arc::new(Mutex::new(HashSet::new())) };\n        // Start supervision without waiting for daemon I/O or expert restoration.\n        if backend.config.isolation == \"shared\" { backend.client()?; }\n        Ok(backend)\n    }\n    fn client(&self) -> anyhow::Result<Arc<Client>> {\n        if self.config.isolation == \"per-account\" { return Err(BackendError::AccountContextRequired.into()); }\n        self.client.get_or_try_init(|| Client::new(self.config.clone())).cloned()\n    }\n    /// Configure a mapped idle session through the protocol's typed public options.\n    pub fn configure_session(&self, key: &str, options: protocol::SessionOptions) -> anyhow::Result<Value> {\n        sessions::configure(self.client()?.as_ref(), key, options)\n    }\n    /// Process-wide configuration; close every session reported by the daemon.\n    pub fn apply_config(&self, config: Option<Value>, credentials: Option<Value>) -> anyhow::Result<Value> {\n        let client = self.client()?;\n        // agentd reopens idle sessions with their existing SessionManager and defers\n        // busy sessions until completion; never abort an in-flight provider switch.\n        let result = client.call(Command::Apply(protocol::Apply { config, credentials }))?;\n        Ok(result)\n    }\n}\nimpl AgentBackend for PiBackend {\n    fn experts_enabled(&self, enabled: Option<bool>) -> anyhow::Result<bool> { self.expert_state(enabled) }\n    fn auth(&self, operation: &str, provider: &str, input: Option<String>) -> anyhow::Result<Value> {\n        self.client()?.call(Command::Auth(protocol::Auth { operation: operation.into(), provider: provider.into(), input }))\n    }\n    fn provider_apply(&self, id: &str) -> anyhow::Result<Value> {\n        let (generation, selected) = crate::provider::selection::snapshot();\n        if selected != id { return Ok(serde_json::json!({\"applied\":false,\"superseded\":true})); }\n        let client = self.client()?;\n        // Serialize deliveries, independently of provider state/queries. Check the\n        // ticket both before sending and after every potentially slow daemon call.\n        let mut last = self.provider_config.lock();\n        let current = || crate::provider::selection::current(generation);\n        let superseded = || serde_json::json!({\"applied\":false,\"superseded\":true});\n        if !current() { return Ok(superseded()); }\n        let catalog = client.call(Command::Catalog(Empty {}));\n        if !current() { return Ok(superseded()); }\n        let catalog = protocol::Catalog::parse(catalog?)?;\n        let config = crate::provider::pi_translate::config(id, &serde_json::to_value(catalog)?).map_err(anyhow::Error::msg)?;\n        let pid = client.status.lock().pid;\n        if !current() { return Ok(superseded()); }\n        if last.as_ref() == Some(&(pid, config.clone())) { return Ok(serde_json::json!({\"applied\":true})); }\n        let result = self.apply_config(Some(config.clone()), None);\n        if !current() { *last = None; return Ok(superseded()); }\n        let result = result?;\n        *last = Some((pid, config));\n        Ok(result)\n    }\n\n    fn permission_respond(&self, response: protocol::PermissionResponse) -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n        self.client()?.call(Command::PermissionRespond(response)).map(|_| ())\n    }\n    fn sandbox_respond(&self, response: protocol::SandboxResponse) -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n        self.client()?.call(Command::SandboxRespond(response)).map(|_| ())\n    }\n    fn start(&self, input: TurnRequest) -> anyhow::Result<EventStream> {\n        self.start_with_tools(input, ToolOptions::default())\n    }\n    fn start_with_tools(&self, input: TurnRequest, options: ToolOptions) -> anyhow::Result<EventStream> {\n        if self.config.isolation == \"per-account\" {\n            return Err(if input.account_id.is_some() { BackendError::UnsupportedIsolation } else { BackendError::AccountContextRequired }.into());\n        }\n        anyhow::ensure!(!input.prompt.trim().is_empty(), \"AgentdEmptyPrompt\");\n        if crate::provider::credential_file::provider_store_path().is_some() {\n            loop {\n                let (_, id) = crate::provider::selection::snapshot();\n                if self.provider_apply(&id)?[\"superseded\"] != true { break; }\n            }\n        }\n        let client = self.client()?;\n        if client.status.lock().circuit_open { return Err(BackendError::CircuitOpen.into()); }\n        let (sender, stream) = stream::Mailbox::channel(self.config.channel_capacity, self.config.max_line_bytes);\n        let preparing = self.preparing.clone();\n        let cancelled = self.cancelled.clone();\n        anyhow::ensure!(preparing.lock().insert(input.req_id.clone()), \"AgentdDuplicateRequest\");\n        let key = format!(\"session:{}\", input.session_id);\n        if !preparing.lock().insert(key.clone()) {\n            preparing.lock().remove(&input.req_id);\n            anyhow::bail!(\"AgentdSessionBusy\");\n        }\n        std::thread::spawn(move || {\n            let req = input.req_id.clone();\n            let conv = input.conversation_id.clone();\n            let mut registered = false;\n            let result = std::panic::catch_unwind(std::panic::AssertUnwindSafe(|| -> anyhow::Result<()> {\n                sender.push_blocking(event(&req, conv.as_deref(), \"meta\",\n                    Some(crate::chat::prompt::estimate_tokens(&input.prompt).to_string())));\n                if cancelled.lock().remove(&req) { sender.finish(None, event(&req, conv.as_deref(), \"done\", None)); return Ok(()); }\n                let detailed_events = options.detailed_events;\n                let info = sessions::open(&client, &input, options)?;\n                if matches!(input.permission, PermissionMode::Deny) {\n                    anyhow::ensure!(info.tools.iter().all(|t| client.config.readonly_tools.contains(t)),\n                        BackendError::UnsupportedInput(\"read-only/manual request cannot use a daemon with write or execution tools\"));\n                }\n                let (tx, rx) = mpsc::sync_channel(1);\n                // Control::Register.timeout is the hard limit; zero means unlimited.\n                let configured_max = Duration::from_millis(client.config.turn_max_ms);\n                // Preserve an explicit zero request budget as immediate expiry,\n                // rather than confusing it with the configured unlimited sentinel.\n                let timeout = match input.timeout.map(|limit| limit.max(Duration::from_nanos(1))) {\n                    Some(limit) if !configured_max.is_zero() => limit.min(configured_max),\n                    Some(limit) => limit,\n                    None => configured_max,\n                };\n                client.send(Control::Register { session: info.id.clone(), req: req.clone(),\n                    translator: translate::Translator::new(req.clone(), conv.clone(), input.cwd.clone(), &client.config)\n                        .with_details(detailed_events)\n                        .with_provider(info.model.get(\"provider\").and_then(Value::as_str).unwrap_or_default()),\n                    stream: sender.clone(), timeout, reservation: (preparing.clone(), key.clone()), reply: tx })?;\n                client.wait(rx)?;\n                registered = true;\n                let result = client.call(Command::Prompt(Prompt {\n                    session_id: info.id.clone(), text: input.prompt, attachments: input.attachments,\n# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n# polaris-kernel — 核心内核 crate(分仓规划 v2 第 2 仓的仓内形态)\n# chat 对话管线 / provider 供应商坞 / doctor 环境医生 / skills 技能框架 /\n# integrations 网关集成 / conv 项目·对话存储 / claude_md 主上下文。\n# 边界铁律: 只准向下依赖 polaris-runtime(横切基建);对检索(kb/fable)与专家团\n#   (expert)的一切需要走 chat::bridges 的 trait 注入(壳侧 wiring 拼装)——\n#   kernel 不认识任何引擎板块,编译器物理保证。\n# 双壳: 默认(无特性)= server 形态(host shim 事件);desktop 特性开 tauri + sandbox。\n# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n[package]\nname = \"polaris-kernel\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2021\"\npublish = false\n\n[dependencies]\npolaris-runtime = { path = \"../polaris-runtime\" }\n# 纯逻辑板块: 看门狗计时核(chat 管线用) / 供应商故障滑窗(provider 坞用)\npolaris-watchdog = { path = \"../polaris-watchdog\" }\npolaris-failover = { path = \"../polaris-failover\" }\n# 版本与主 crate 逐条对齐(同 workspace 共享编译产物,零增量)\nserde = { version = \"1\", features = [\"derive\"] }\nserde_json = \"1\"\nanyhow = \"1\"\nonce_cell = \"1\"\nparking_lot = \"0.12\"\ndirectories = \"5\"\nwalkdir = \"2\"\nregex = \"1\"\nbase64 = \"0.22\"\nureq = { version = \"2\", features = [\"json\"] }\n# Claude 订阅 OAuth(PKCE)+ Codex 设备码流程(provider/)\nsha2 = \"0.10\"\ngetrandom = \"0.2\"\nchrono = { version = \"0.4\", default-features = false, features = [\"clock\"] }\nzip = \"8.6.0\"\ntokio = { version = \"1\", features = [\"time\", \"macros\", \"rt-multi-thread\", \"sync\", \"net\", \"io-util\", \"signal\", \"process\"] }\n# 文件转换 convert.rs(chat 附件 + kb/fable 入库共用, 收在内核, 上层引擎向下取用)\ncalamine = \"0.35.0\"\npdf-extract = \"0.10.0\"\n# integrations/nas.rs: GBK 文件名解码\nencoding_rs = \"0.8\"\n# 飞书建应用二维码(integrations/feishu)\nqrcode = { version = \"0.14\", default-features = false, features = [\"svg\"] }\ntauri = { version = \"2.1\", features = [], optional = true }\n\n[target.'cfg(windows)'.dependencies]\nwindows-sys = { version = \"0.59\", features = [\"Win32_Foundation\", \"Win32_Graphics_Dwm\", \"Win32_Storage_FileSystem\", \"Win32_System_Diagnostics_Debug\", \"Win32_System_WindowsProgramming\", \"Win32_NetworkManagement_WNet\", \"Win32_System_SystemInformation\", \"Win32_System_Diagnostics_ToolHelp\", \"Win32_System_Threading\", \"Win32_System_JobObjects\", \"Win32_Security\"] }\n\n[target.'cfg(unix)'.dependencies]\nlibc = \"0.2\"\n\n[features]\ndefault = []\ndesktop = [\"dep:tauri\"]\n# Polaris 功能树（P1–P3 接线进展）\n\n2026-10-14 · `refactor/pi-agent`。未迁移节点的行号沿用 `0be46d7` 静态基线；P2 节点以当前文件为准。\n原静态基线保留；P2 更新了 chat/headless/壳注册路径，实际检查与未完成项见 [P2 记录](pi-migration/p2-result.md)。\n迁移明细见 [调用点](pi-migration/call-sites.md)、[事件契约](pi-migration/agent-events.md)、[超长文件](pi-migration/oversized-files.md)。\n\n## 路径、测试与依赖记法\n\n`K/`=`src-tauri/crates/polaris-kernel/src/`；`F/`=`src-tauri/crates/polaris-fable/src/`；`W/`=`src-tauri/crates/polaris-wiki/src/`。\n`C/`=`src-tauri/crates/polaris-collab/src/`；`S/`=`src-tauri/crates/polaris-sandbox/src/`；`H/`=`src-tauri/src/`。\n箭头 `A→B` 表示 A 编译依赖或调用 B，桥接回调另行说明，不能把运行时注入误写成 crate 互引。\n\n| 测试代号 | 命令 / 依据 |\n| --- | --- |\n| K | 在 `src-tauri/` 执行 `cargo test -p polaris-kernel --lib --tests`；CI 单独跑内核以避免 desktop/server 特性合并（`.github/workflows/ci.yml:35,44,46`） |\n| F / W | 在 `src-tauri/` 执行 `cargo test -p polaris-fable` / `cargo test -p polaris-wiki`；包定义分别 `src-tauri/crates/polaris-fable/Cargo.toml:9`、`src-tauri/crates/polaris-wiki/Cargo.toml:8`；真实模型/数据评测另有开关，不能算普通测试已覆盖 |\n| C | 在 `src-tauri/` 执行 `cargo test -p polaris-collab --features c